     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Block fileServer:lateralMovement, domainAdmin:privilegeEscalation and hypervisor:privilegeEscalation. (1) Blocking fileServer cuts codeRepo, since its other parent secretsManager is an AND step that also needs fileServer. That also cuts vaultRead and the secretsManager branch of dbReplica. (2) Blocking domainAdmin cuts mailArchive and the domainAdmin branch of dbReplica. (3) Blocking hypervisor cuts the last branch of dbReplica. Two blocks cannot work because the target has three independent ways in. First, fileServer is reachable via tokenCache, which is fed directly by footholds. Second, domainAdmin is reachable via apiToken and rdpLogin. Third, hypervisor is reachable via configSecret, monitoringHost, vpnSession and printServer. No single step lies on more than one of these three, so each needs its own block.\"}"
    }
   ],
